From 49f9c19df2b7157594498eb81091c8f4c6dbdbf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 03:32:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: reset the clock gracefully instead of aborting at the
 threshold

borg_think_dungeon() aborted the borg with borg_oops("clock
overflow") once borg.time.now reached BORG_TIME_MAX - 3000. The
graceful clock reset in borg_think() only fires at BORG_TIME_MAX -
100, so the abort always won about 2900 turns earlier and the graceful
reset was unreachable: an aborted borg never thinks again, the clock
never advances, and the only handler the borg ever exercised was the
panic.

Reset the clock in place (the same borg.time.now = 1 assignment the
borg_think() overflow check performs) and keep playing; borg_think()'s
check remains as a failsafe in case the reset is somehow missed.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#246.

(cherry picked from commit 7cc0ebbd2016afeaaf57c5e976251b67f7c0e147)
---
 src/borg/borg-think-dungeon.c | 14 ++++++++------
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon.c b/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon.c
index 33a343aef..a3dd50f89 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-think-dungeon.c
@@ -1287,13 +1287,15 @@ bool borg_think_dungeon(void)
         return true;
     }
 
-    /* Prevent clock wrapping Step 2 */
+    /* Prevent clock wrapping Step 2: reset the clock gracefully and keep
+     * playing.  This must run before any panic: the borg_think() overflow
+     * check remains as a failsafe in case the reset was somehow missed.
+     * The previous version aborted the borg here, which fired about 2900
+     * turns earlier than the reset threshold and made the graceful reset
+     * unreachable. */
     if (borg.time.now >= BORG_TIME_MAX - 3000) {
-        /* Panic */
-        borg_oops("clock overflow");
-
-        /* Oops */
-        return true;
+        borg.time.now = 1;
+        borg_warning("*****WARNING***** Borg Clock Overflow");
     }
 
     /* no longer trying an unknown object */
